  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a classical quantum‑inspired genetic algorithm (MQIGA) using simulated qudit states and decoherence. On benchmark optimization functions (n=2 and n=15), MQIGA reaches the global optimum in up to 100% of runs and shows faster convergence than GA, DE, PSO, and QIGA baselines; it also improves regression accuracy in ELM tuning (e.g., MAE 1.86 on Boston Housing vs 3.35 for standard ELM). All experiments run on a classical CPU (Intel Core i9‑13980HX) with no gate‑based quantum hardware.",
